* "German Quad" (a four-channel 100 W German head of the Diezel VH4 kind), preamp, channel 1 (the main netlist; channels 2 to 4 are stage_ch2.net .. stage_ch4.net, then stage_out.net),
* transcribed from the supplied drawing (VH4 classic, SCH000, 28.05.2005: red values are the drawing's, crossed-out parts are not fitted, parts with a red bar are bridged).
* The four channels share V1A and the V2A gain stage with the V2B cathode follower; the relays pick what reaches V2A's input: ST1 channel 1 (GAIN 1), else ST3 / ST4 choose
* between channel 2 (M1) and the common tube Tc, which takes channel 3 (GAIN 3, ST3) or channel 4 (GAIN 4 and Tb, ST4). Each channel has its own tone stack and VOLUME after
* the follower, and ST1 .. ST4 put the selected VOLUME onto the bus (stage_out.net).
* Here each channel is one netlist with its own copy of the shared tubes (only the selected channel is solved). Not modelled: the mute, the channel inserts, the MIX pot and the
* loops (one gain stage stands in for the loop buffers in stage_out.net), the DEEP control.

V VRAIL x 100 400
R R86 x dp 15k
C C87 dp 0 10u
I VIN gin 1
R RSRC gin in 7k
R RPU1 gin pkb1 1e12
.xfmr LPU1 L=2.5
  W pkb1 in 1 pu
.end
R RPU2 gin pkb2 1e12
.xfmr LPU2 L=5
  W pkb2 in 1 pu
.end
C CPU gin in 110p
R RPL gin in 1e12
R SWK1 in pkk1 1e12
C CCAB1 pkk1 0 200p
R SWK2 in pkk2 1e12
C CCAB2 pkk2 0 400p
R SWK4 in pkk4 1e12
C CCAB4 pkk4 0 800p

* V1A: 1M and 100p to ground, the 68k stopper (the input capacitor is bridged on the drawing), 1k2 with 10u on the cathode, 120k plate load.
R R1M in 0 1M
C C100P in 0 100p
R R68K in g1 68k
T V1A g1 p1 k1 12AX7
R R1K2 k1 0 1.2k
C C10U k1 0 10u
R R120A dp p1 120k

* CH1: 22n, the bright network (470k with 220p across, 470k to ground at b, a second 470k with 220p, 22p across both; the BRIGHT switch adds 68p), GAIN 1 (220k-A
* wiper pot) with 220k at its wiper g, which ST1 brings to h.
C C22N p1 a 22n
R RB1 a b 470k
C CB1 a b 220p
R RSH1 b 0 470k
R RB2 b e 470k
C CB2 b e 220p
C C22P a e 22p
C C68P a br1 68p
R SW_BR1 br1 e 1e12
R VRG_T e g 1
R VRG_B g 0 1
R R220G g 0 220k
R RST1 g h 1

* The input of the next stage (R470H 470k into V2A's grid and its input capacitance, about 110 pF), repeated here so the cut at h keeps its load; the rail
* resistor above is scaled by (the channel's current / this stage's current) so the plates sit where they did in one netlist.
R RDUM h hd 470k
C CDUM hd 0 110p
